[{:db/id "q-336411/field-1/3d0e9fc312a846a9fe3664c8bb1b8fb48d1e87f08a1cab20be30cba0efd89fbf" :answer/id #uuid "fa3c5cc7-71fb-5010-ad6b-1a533546701c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12t^2-4t+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336411/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9673dbbd-04cf-5b77-9aaf-b2620c4dcaac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336411/field-1/3d0e9fc312a846a9fe3664c8bb1b8fb48d1e87f08a1cab20be30cba0efd89fbf" :answer-field/choices ["q-336411/field-1/3d0e9fc312a846a9fe3664c8bb1b8fb48d1e87f08a1cab20be30cba0efd89fbf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336411" :question/id #uuid "a5d4ebd2-81c0-5bff-9a4f-770afd89a880" :question/math-academy-id "q-336411" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=4{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+9t.$ Calculate the acceleration $a$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+9t) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-4t+9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336411/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336411"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102616/selection/ff72013971aa4bd34338b3e299ff11bb9b89e6ef5d5892a6f2fafb3952bb35ba" :answer/id #uuid "56bbcfbe-a146-5248-a9ab-6fa3328e0f2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102616/selection/183d9251b39783d1c2251fcef1732c1b684971f2a1e9e8e6abd79f15a6aff7cf" :answer/id #uuid "89626065-c358-5daa-bfdb-9e9ad965be20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102616/selection/efb4f776698e70ba708659fa4660be754f72cba555654d50b3060e615202e50a" :answer/id #uuid "c4df6798-8140-5760-b202-e3fb228bcd5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102616/selection/62b07491e22a681aaa6575b9430bf8bda1d0d8a4de4c052ff936db8771ca7554" :answer/id #uuid "257b3300-0dd0-575a-abf9-ad85c418949b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4e\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102616/selection/d01c3ce5e7dfa801e3265608fad78569c41095ed83a12d1eed5ef726cdc95c73" :answer/id #uuid "8487d8ae-99df-550e-b1e2-4e961f181430" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5e\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102616/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "634c92dc-28e2-5d94-a251-4d66982ec073" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102616/selection/d01c3ce5e7dfa801e3265608fad78569c41095ed83a12d1eed5ef726cdc95c73" :answer-field/choices ["q-102616/selection/ff72013971aa4bd34338b3e299ff11bb9b89e6ef5d5892a6f2fafb3952bb35ba" "q-102616/selection/183d9251b39783d1c2251fcef1732c1b684971f2a1e9e8e6abd79f15a6aff7cf" "q-102616/selection/efb4f776698e70ba708659fa4660be754f72cba555654d50b3060e615202e50a" "q-102616/selection/62b07491e22a681aaa6575b9430bf8bda1d0d8a4de4c052ff936db8771ca7554" "q-102616/selection/d01c3ce5e7dfa801e3265608fad78569c41095ed83a12d1eed5ef726cdc95c73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102616" :question/id #uuid "fb90cea8-c194-5f3c-8376-493a94dba4ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-102616" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=(t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+4t).$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $6\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+4t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1+4 \\\\  & =5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=6,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t & =1 \\\\ {e}^{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)} & ={e}^{1} \\\\ t & =e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=e,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(e) & =(e\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+4e) \\\\  & =e(1)+4e \\\\  & =5e\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=6\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $5e\\text{ m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102616/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102616"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-315537/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c0943335-10f4-58f4-a867-9fc0124f9f86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-315537/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd921af4-aae4-5aef-a9bc-38b09efbfd86" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-315537/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-315537/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-315537" :question/id #uuid "fa61f090-9a51-53fc-9eb9-ce631e6c3c5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-315537" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}.$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nWhen $a=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ the velocity is $v=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2t+1}{2\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=\\frac{1}{2},$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{2t+1}{2\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{2t+1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7} & =2t+1 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7})}^{2} & ={(2t+1)}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+7 & =4{t}^{2}+4t+1 \\\\ 0 & =3{t}^{2}+3t-6 \\\\ 0 & ={t}^{2}+t-2 \\\\ 0 & =(t-1)(t+2) \\\\ t & =1,\\,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $t=1$ since $t\\ge 0.$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=1,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+1+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+7} \\\\  & =3\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $v=3\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-315537/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-315537"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-2361/selection/b4f8666a7b61e5b7908366e9fa365f4b483ae529510c32bb8aa3d1d07d5bf67e" :answer/id #uuid "a339a6f0-0f50-5a18-a092-07b100d1f732" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2361/selection/54634c2d00c6379bd397b85d3d9384efc1a7f95206224cee2aa9dc21bce388b3" :answer/id #uuid "00589345-22ca-5843-9e6f-7da2c12880b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2361/selection/635480935000bab14ea2e2013c48ae8184055739578f539bf95730f53d533797" :answer/id #uuid "374a0e08-4030-591f-b937-d9f89ca1de5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2361/selection/4cae11c65b26a32627d4e5094d0deb244d430f0d520a18f502959e9910126c92" :answer/id #uuid "fe2c33dc-a25e-5115-821d-2a488578c7c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2361/selection/9b82054e069ad052ea81b72efe81172644f90ad4382dc8c17056e6ba37883b7b" :answer/id #uuid "9fa23b08-3989-592a-a7ca-6b270f384213" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2361/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4cd1abc5-3394-5abf-95f2-d520b095aff0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-2361/selection/635480935000bab14ea2e2013c48ae8184055739578f539bf95730f53d533797" :answer-field/choices ["q-2361/selection/b4f8666a7b61e5b7908366e9fa365f4b483ae529510c32bb8aa3d1d07d5bf67e" "q-2361/selection/54634c2d00c6379bd397b85d3d9384efc1a7f95206224cee2aa9dc21bce388b3" "q-2361/selection/635480935000bab14ea2e2013c48ae8184055739578f539bf95730f53d533797" "q-2361/selection/4cae11c65b26a32627d4e5094d0deb244d430f0d520a18f502959e9910126c92" "q-2361/selection/9b82054e069ad052ea81b72efe81172644f90ad4382dc8c17056e6ba37883b7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2361" :question/id #uuid "0b4e7ffe-863b-5593-af94-6129cf7fb536" :question/math-academy-id "q-2361" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=4{t}^{2}-16t+15.$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $0\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}-16t+15) \\\\  & =8t-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=0,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =8t-16 \\\\ 8t & =16 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=2,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =4(2)^{2}-16(2)+15 \\\\  & =16-32+15 \\\\  & =-1\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=0\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $-1\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-2361/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2361"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336415/field-1/b732f6f9c92291a93d2872d55c98972d90a6d95b2c5199ef782a93bda27ffe01" :answer/id #uuid "0c20258f-2a0b-536b-9bad-91fa23c21b8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-\\frac{2}{t^2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336415/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7452ce5f-f87e-5225-8bf5-cca2914bd318" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336415/field-1/b732f6f9c92291a93d2872d55c98972d90a6d95b2c5199ef782a93bda27ffe01" :answer-field/choices ["q-336415/field-1/b732f6f9c92291a93d2872d55c98972d90a6d95b2c5199ef782a93bda27ffe01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336415" :question/id #uuid "e5707e23-6e97-5306-b715-e95fd1fbb831" :question/math-academy-id "q-336415" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{3{t}^{2}-5t+2}{t}.$ Calculate the acceleration $a$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3{t}^{2}-5t+2}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-5+\\frac{2}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-5+2{t}^{-1}) \\\\  & =3+2(-{t}^{-2}) \\\\  & =3-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336415/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336415"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336441/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "7e7851bb-80bf-541c-b821-f1c5dd419b2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336441/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdac6615-f739-5a3d-8a79-8fa482126b15" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336441/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-336441/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336441" :question/id #uuid "565b31b4-2cd1-5b24-8e88-4ac0f4ecf026" :question/math-academy-id "q-336441" :question/problem "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the time when the particle's acceleration is equal to $a=70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nThe acceleration is $70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at\n$t=$\n{{field-1}} seconds." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12{t}^{2}-2t) \\\\  & =24t-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=70,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}70 & =24t-2 \\\\ 24t & =72 \\\\ t & =3\\text{ }\\text{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is $70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at $t=3$ seconds." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336441/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336441"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336448/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer/id #uuid "04070d84-002d-5243-88f2-eb78a5f072c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336448/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "ecc89e46-066b-54d0-9afe-53af32fb2a90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336448/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "358ba194-bb39-51d4-a3e6-ee8747dadba5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336448/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer-field/choices ["q-336448/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" "q-336448/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336448" :question/id #uuid "a67b4607-4f56-5bb6-afe2-1f29e415c471" :question/math-academy-id "q-336448" :question/problem "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=5{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the particle's acceleration at $t=1$ second.\n\n$a(1)=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =15{t}^{2}-4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(15{t}^{2}-4t) \\\\  & =30t-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=1$ second, we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =30(1)-4 \\\\  & =26\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336448/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336448"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-2359"] :question/problem "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=4{t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}-15$, where $t$ is measured in seconds.  Find the particle's acceleration at $t=3$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}+20t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12{t}^{2}+20t) \\\\  & =24t+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=3$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(3) & =24(3)+20 \\\\  & =72+20 \\\\  & =92\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=3$ seconds is $92\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-336459/field-1/f896f59ba4eef65a56abf248c9ea3c4544bbe2ca1270d2c0acd95ce5c2d617d7" :answer/id #uuid "5e60107a-c998-5ae7-a420-1edf435880bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\cos(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336459/field-1/b45db07090fca75d2c63f4a6fba9ba932f3d1334146dacfb9c1d0c69b00cd77e" :answer/id #uuid "b497b5a7-5305-5068-a36e-5ecc68200ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\cos(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336459/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "598b8183-067e-511b-9b1d-c5b8485396a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336459/field-1/f896f59ba4eef65a56abf248c9ea3c4544bbe2ca1270d2c0acd95ce5c2d617d7" :answer-field/choices ["q-336459/field-1/f896f59ba4eef65a56abf248c9ea3c4544bbe2ca1270d2c0acd95ce5c2d617d7" "q-336459/field-1/b45db07090fca75d2c63f4a6fba9ba932f3d1334146dacfb9c1d0c69b00cd77e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336459" :question/id #uuid "444c1907-febd-59a8-aae6-a4e212ab81e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-336459" :question/problem "The displacement $s$ of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t).$ Find the particle's acceleration at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336459/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336459"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336449/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "ae4bbbe4-a959-53d8-8d1f-ab71a8b69ebe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336449/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "eba84d2c-0c78-563a-8459-dfac8d2a5232" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336449/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-336449/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336449" :question/id #uuid "155a0fbe-b5fe-59e5-9db0-2a3a6209eb2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-336449" :question/problem "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=2{t}^{4}-{t}^{2}+3t,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the particle's acceleration at $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ second.\n\n$a(\\frac{1}{2})=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}-{t}^{2}+3t) \\\\  & =8{t}^{3}-2t+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8{t}^{3}-2t+3) \\\\  & =24{t}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ second, we substitute $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(\\frac{1}{2}) & =24{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2 \\\\  & =24\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-2 \\\\  & =4\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336449/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336449"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-215"] :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-6t-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-6-6t \\\\  & =-6(1+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-216"] :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $x(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t+3{t}^{2}+4{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =2+6t+12{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+6t+12{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6+24t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=0$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =6+24(0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=0$ is $6$." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
